## Type lookup (ImplementationPlan.md 5.11.4, M21.b item 2; texts of
## 5.11.9). The candidates for a name are the public TypeDefs with exactly
## that full name; a nested type counts only when every enclosing type is
## public or nested-public:
## - one candidate binds (Fake.Widget: FakeTypesB's is not public);
## - two are 'type '<Ns.Type>' is defined in two references: <identity> (<path>) and <identity> (<path>)',
##   with the same text in either reference order (Fake.Dup);
## - three or more (section 12 row 2026-10-26, '5.11.9 clarified (three or
##   more candidates)') are 'type '<Ns.Type>' is defined in <n> references: <list>',
##   <n> in digits and every candidate as '<identity> (<path>)' in
##   ReferenceSet's rank order (the identity text ignoring case), joined by
##   ', ' with ' and ' before the last, in either reference order (Fake.Dup
##   with FakeTypesC, FakeTypesB.il's variant TYPES_C, besides);
## - a nested type binds through its enclosing type (Fake.Outer/Inner from
##   FakeTypesA; FakeTypesB's has a non-public enclosing type, and its
##   Fake.Box/Inner is nested-private, so neither counts);
## - a generic type's name carries its arity (Fake.Gen`1; Fake.Gen is not
##   defined);
## - nothing is 'type '<Ns.Type>' is not defined in the references (<n> assemblies)'.
## Phase 2 makes no request for such types, so the lookup is reached through
## msil-ld's hidden --print-bcl-binding=type:<Ns>.<Name>[/<Nested>] (5.11.5),
## which prints '<request> -> <result>' (the bound type or the error text).
## Each request runs on its own, so that its whole output is checked. The
## links themselves need nothing from the references (ret42.o).
## A link that binds an ambiguous type fails the same way: fence.o's
## Interlocked::MemoryBarrier finds Interlocked in FakeThreading and in
## System.Private.FakeLib.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj ret42.ll -o ret42.o
# RUN: mkdir ab b
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeTypesA.yaml -o ab/FakeTypesA.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeTypesB.yaml -o ab/FakeTypesB.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeTypesB.yaml -o b/FakeTypesB.dll

# DEFINE: %{bind} = msil-ld ret42.o --reference=FakeCore.dll --reference=ab -o out.exe
# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR" --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=warning:
# DEFINE: %{bound} = %{fc} --implicit-check-not="defined in two" --implicit-check-not="not defined"

## One public definition.
# RUN: %{bind} --print-bcl-binding=type:Fake.Widget 2>&1 | %{bound} --check-prefix=WIDGET --implicit-check-not=FakeTypesB
# WIDGET: {{^}}type:Fake.Widget -> {{.*(FakeTypesA.*Fake.Widget|Fake.Widget.*FakeTypesA).*$}}
# RUN: %{bind} --print-bcl-binding=type:System.Object 2>&1 | %{bound} --check-prefix=OBJECT --implicit-check-not=FakeTypes
# OBJECT: {{^}}type:System.Object -> {{.*(FakeCore.*System.Object|System.Object.*FakeCore).*$}}

## Two public definitions, in either order of the references.
# RUN: %{bind} --print-bcl-binding=type:Fake.Dup > dup-ab.txt 2>&1
# RUN: msil-ld ret42.o --reference=ab/FakeTypesB.dll --reference=ab/FakeTypesA.dll --reference=FakeCore.dll \
# RUN:   --print-bcl-binding=type:Fake.Dup -o out.exe > dup-ba.txt 2>&1
# RUN: %{fc} --check-prefix=DUP --input-file=dup-ab.txt
# RUN: diff dup-ab.txt dup-ba.txt
# DUP: {{^}}type:Fake.Dup -> type 'Fake.Dup' is defined in two references: {{(.*FakeTypesA.* \(.*\) and .*FakeTypesB.* \(.*\)|.*FakeTypesB.* \(.*\) and .*FakeTypesA.* \(.*\))$}}

## Three public definitions, in either order of the references.
